{{Top}}
{{Quote|Without a doubt, the pirate is the greatest of all those who work beyond the boundaries of what most consider to be legal. They have earned an unfair reputation as cheats and brigands, but I see them as nothing more than independent businesspeople operating outside of an unjust system. Pirates tend to work in gangs, most of which are run by charming captains who lead their crews to glory with unmatched savvy and unwavering vision. But even though the captain calls the shots, true pirates serve no master but themselves, taking only the jobs that benefit them the most.|Hondo Ohnaka, Pirate King|<ref name="SotBH">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Bounty Hunters]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Pirates-SWGoH.png|thumb|right|300px|Pirates existed throughout the galaxy.]]
'''Pirates''',<ref name="Hunt on Celsor 3">{{Resistance|Hunt on Celsor 3}}</ref> also known as '''space pirates''',<ref name="I229">{{InsiderCite|229|Star Wars: Skeleton Crew: Join the Crew|''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'': Join the Crew}}</ref> were individuals who engaged in the criminal activity known as '''piracy'''. Such acts included hunting,<ref name="Hunt on Celsor 3" /> hostage taking,<ref name="Dooku Captured">{{TCW|Dooku Captured}}</ref> and theft of cargo.<ref name="A Test of Strength">{{TCW|A Test of Strength}}</ref> Notable pirates include [[Hondo Ohnaka]] who had dealings with the highest levels of leadership of both the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]], and those led by [[Q'anah (pirate)|Q'anah]], who was thwarted by [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] during his tenure with the [[Outland Regions Security Force]] of [[Eriadu]]. Pirates were sometimes associated with [[bounty hunter]]s.<ref name="Lethal Trackdown">{{TCW|Lethal Trackdown}}</ref>

Pirates were in a similar class of galactic individuals like [[smuggler]]s, [[fringer]]s, and scoundrels.<ref name="TROSVD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Pirates who were legitimized by a [[letter of marque]]<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref> from some government or authority were known as [[privateer]]s.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> Piracy was often romanticized in media and popular culture, where it was associated with the perceived freedom that came from breaking the rules.<ref name="Scum">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref>

==History==
===Age of the Republic===
====Republic's reign====
{{Quote|We go where we want. We strike where we want. Our will is the only authority in this part of the galaxy, and the only one there ever will be. I do not wish to rule the galaxy. If I did, you would be under my boot even now. But I will take what I wish, when I wish it, and no one will stand in my way&mdash;Republic, Jedi, or anyone else.|Eye of the Nihil Marchion Ro|<ref name="Fallen Star">''[[The High Republic: The Fallen Star]]''</ref>}}
[[File:PiratesHetzal.png|thumb|right|250px|Pirate attack on [[Hetzal Prime]]]]
Prior to the construction of [[starship]]s that pirates could prey upon, they hunted a vast array of creatures, such as [[purrgil]] and [[Exogorth|space slugs]].<ref name="Hunt on Celsor 3" /><ref name="Preview">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-hunt-on-celsor-3-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 9 Fun Facts from "Hunt on Celsor 3" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> The [[Nihil]] emerged as a major threat to the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[High Republic Era]]: the marauders were responsible for major atrocities, including the [[Great Hyperspace Disaster]] through their [[Path|unique travel]] in [[hyperspace]],<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> the [[Valo Atrocity|attack]] on the [[Republic Fair]]<ref name="The Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref> and numerous other raids, and even the [[Destruction of Starlight Beacon|destruction]] of the [[Starlight Beacon]].<ref name="Fallen Star" /> The [[Eye of the Nihil]], [[Marchion Ro]], would even establish the [[Occlusion Zone|Nihil space]] and claimed he did so in the name of creating a place free of Republic rule.<ref name="Eye of the Storm 2">[[The High Republic: Eye of the Storm 2|''The High Republic: Eye of the Storm'' 2]]</ref>

Before the [[Invasion of Naboo]], [[Lord]] [[Alorg]]'s [[Flesh Mongers]] kidnapped a child, [[Lo]]. However they lost the child when Jedi [[Grand Master]] Yoda [[Rescue of Lo|rescued]] Lo.<ref name="SW26">[[Star Wars (2015) 26|''Star Wars'' (2015) 26]]</ref> Another [[Unidentified pirate faction|pirate faction]] carried out numerous raids on [[Trade Federation]].<ref name="Darth Maul 1">[[Darth Maul (2017) 1|''Darth Maul'' (2017) 1]]</ref> [[Nym]] and his [[Lok Revenants]] were pirates who targeted the Trade Federation, [[spicerunner]]s, and [[enslaver]]s, and sometimes worked with the [[Jedi Master]] [[Adi Gallia]]. Following the [[Battle of Naboo]], [[Hudso Shaku]] and his [[Krypder Riders]] attempted to steal a [[Jedi holocron|Jedi]] [[Dallenor holocron|holocron]] from a [[Dallenor Excavation|excavation]] on [[Dallenor]]. However, they failed due to intervention from Jedi Master [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]].<ref name="AoR-OWK1">[[Age of Republic - Obi-Wan Kenobi 1|''Age of Republic - Obi-Wan Kenobi'' 1]]</ref>

====Clone Wars====
{{Quote|Filth...you will pay for your insolence.''"''<br />''"''Insolence? We are pirates! We don't even know what that means!|Maul and Hondo Ohnaka|<ref name="Revival">{{TCW|Revival (episode)}}</ref>}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], several Republic supply ships were destroyed by pirates en route to [[Rodia]].<ref name="Bombad Jedi">{{TCW|Bombad Jedi}}</ref> Later the pirate [[Ohnaka Gang|gang]] of Captain [[Hondo Ohnaka]] captured Separatist leader, [[Count]] [[Dooku]] on [[Vanqor]]. They attempted to ransom Dooku off to the Republic.<ref name="Dooku Captured" /> They tried to triple the ransom by capturing Jedi Master Kenobi and Jedi Knight Skywalker. However, Dooku escaped and Kenobi and Skywalker were rescued by Representative [[Jar Jar Binks]] and [[Clone Commander]] [[Stone (clone trooper)|Stone's]] troopers.<ref name="Gungan General">{{TCW|The Gungan General}}</ref> The Ohnaka Gang would continue in their operations such as extorting [[nysillin]] from farmers on [[Felucia]],<ref name="Bounty Hunters">{{TCW|Bounty Hunters (episode)}}</ref> smuggling weapons to known resistance movements,<ref name="Tipping Points">{{TCW|Tipping Points}}</ref> and attempted to steal [[Kyber crystal]]s from a group of [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]].<ref name="A Test of Strength" />

[[File:Ohnaka_pirate_gang.png|thumb|left|250px|The Ohnaka gang]]
Several members of the Ohnaka gang were approached and bribed by [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] and his brother [[Savage Opress]] into working for them. [[Jiro]] and several of the pirates joined Maul until Captain Ohnaka was able to hold them at gunpoint. The Ohnaka gang along with Master Kenobi were able to force the two zabraks to retreat. After Maul's ship crashed, the Ohnaka gang found the [[credit coffer]] and assumed that the Zabraks were dead.<ref name="Revival" /> Another group of Weequay pirates of the [[Marauder (Weequay pirate ship)|''Marauder'']] organized [[gladiator]] games aboard their ship with stolen droids.<ref name="Nomad Droids">{{TCW|Nomad Droids}}</ref>

At some unspecified point of her life, [[Kiera Swan]] became a pirate and became well known in [[the galaxy]]. However, she later abandoned that occupation and became a [[bounty hunter]], something which made her more famous than she was before.<ref name="TB">{{TCW|The Box}}</ref>

[[Lassa Rhayme]] [[Pantoran]] [[pirate]] who served as the [[captain]] of the ''[[Opportunity]]'' and "[[Pirate Queen]]" leader of the [[Blood Bone Order]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. During the last months of the war, she had an encounter with [[bounty hunter]] [[Asajj Ventress]], whom she considered a friend after successfully recovering the ''[[Steady On]]'' and its cargo from Hondo Ohnaka and his gang on their own.<ref name="Kindred Spirits">{{InsiderCite|159|Kindred Spirits}}</ref>

===Age of the Empire===
====Empire's reign====
[[File:EnfysAndBeckett-Beckett1.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The Cloud Riders interrogating Tobias Beckett]]
According to reports from the [[Imperial Security Bureau]], pirate groups were likely to shelter in the polar regions. In order to keep control of such regions, [[Imperial High Command]] established the [[Cold weather assault trooper|snowtrooper]] division.<ref name="Imperial Troops">{{EncyclopediaCite|Imperial Troops}}</ref> [[Phee Genoa]] was a pirate operating in the early Imperial Era.<ref name="Spoils of War">{{TBB|Spoils of War}}</ref> The Empire was able to break up the Ohnaka gang, but Ohnaka continued with his operations on his own.<ref name="Brothers of the Broken Horn">{{Rebels|Brothers of the Broken Horn}}</ref> [[Enfys Nest]] and her [[Cloud-Riders]] were seen as pirates during their attempted thefts of [[Identichip]]s<ref name="Beckett">[[Beckett 1|''Beckett'' 1]]</ref> and [[Coaxium]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Gwarm, formerly Ohnaka's lieutenant, started his own [[Gwarm's gang|gang]].<ref name="Droid Hunters">[[Star Wars Adventures Free Comic Book Day 2019|''Star Wars Adventures'' Free Comic Book Day 2019]]</ref> The Empire fought with the [[Iska pirates]] during the Imperial Era.<ref name="The Secret Academy">''[[Servants of the Empire: The Secret Academy]]''</ref>

[[Angel (pirate)|Angel's]] [[Culoss]] band hijacked the freighter ''[[Dromedar]]'' to steal its [[tibanna]] [[gas]] and captured its crew. The Culoss pretended to be its crew when a boarding party under Lieutenant [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] from the Imperial Navy ship ''[[Blood Crow]]''. They were able to capture the boarding party and escape with the gas. However, three of the pirates were captured and questioned by Thrawn at [[Ansion]]'s [[Unidentified Imperial base (Ansion)|Imperial base]]. With Thrawn's information, the Culoss' operations on [[Uba]], [[Cartherston]], and [[Kril'Dor]] were targeted by the Empire.<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref>

Ohnaka was able to briefly take [[Cikatro Vizago]]'s ship, the ''[[Broken Horn]]'' and take [[Azmorigan]]'s credits for the [[power generator]]. Ohnaka lost the ship, however, when Bridger helped Vizago in taking back the ''Broken Horn''. He was able to keep the credits for himself.<ref name="Brothers of the Broken Horn" /> Ohnaka helped the [[Spectres]] of [[Phoenix Cell]] in rescuing Lasat refugees,<ref name="Legends of the Lasat">{{Rebels|Legends of the Lasat}}</ref> providing locations of derelict bombers<ref name="Steps Into Shadow">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''</ref> and acquiring [[proton bomb]]s. He also recruited [[Melch]] as a partner.<ref name="Wynkahthu Job">{{Rebels|The Wynkahthu Job}}</ref> The [[Seventh Fleet (Galactic Empire)|Seventh]] and [[Third Fleet]]s hunted down pirates that were causing problems for [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]]'s [[Project Stardust]]. Thrawn discovered that Savit was working with the pirates in stealing supplies Governor [[Haveland]] and Krennic. Thrawn was able to defeat Savit's fleet and had him tried for treason on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Treason">''[[Thrawn: Treason]]''</ref>

====Galactic Civil War====
During the [[Galactic Civil War]], Vader dealt with [[Crymorah-backed pirates|pirates]] backed by the [[Crymorah Syndicate]].<ref name="Vader II">[[Darth Vader (2015) 2|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 2]]</ref> The [[Krawg pirates]] attempted to buy a crate of Imperial [[E-11 medium blaster rifle|blasters]] from smuggler [[Sana Starros]]. However, Starros tricked them and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] made sure the pirates were arrested by the Empire for the theft.<ref name="13 crates">[[Star Wars (2015) 34|''Star Wars'' (2015) 34]]</ref> During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], Rhayme and her Blood Bone Order became a food and weapons supplier for a subgroup of the mainly extinct [[Partisans]] known as the [[Dreamers]].<ref name="Inferno Squad">''[[Battlefront II: Inferno Squad]]''</ref>

Following the end of the Civil War, [[Eleodie Maracavanya]] and zher pirates of the [[Sovereign Latitudes of Maracavanya]] were able to capture the [[Executor-class Star Dreadnought|''Executor''-class Star Dreadnought]] [[Liberty's Misrule|''Annihilator'']] and renamed it the ''Liberty's Misrule''.<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> Together, Maracavany and zher pirates used it to control their small empire in [[Wild Space]].<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> Another pirate, [[Viz Moshara]] attempted to protect [[Substation Grimdock]] from the [[New Republic army]], but was killed.<ref name="Last Shot">''[[Last Shot]]''</ref>

===Age of the New Republic===
{{Quote|Kid. Never trust a pirate.|Din Djarin to Grogu|<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>}}
By the time of the [[New Republic]], they could not stop the [[Pirate Nation]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]]. [[Gorian Shard]] and his [[Gorian Shard's pirate crew|gang]] attacked [[Nevarro]], but eventually were defeated by [[Mandalorian]]s.<ref name="Chapter 21">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref>

[[File:Silvos_pirates.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A pirate crew under the command of Silvo.]]
On the other hand, in the [[Outer Rim Territories]], many pirates settled at the [[Borgo Prime]] base, located in the [[Hydian Way]]. A widespread myth among many pirates from this era is that of [[At Attin]], a lost world where legendary treasure was believed to lie, a pirate's dream. Captain "[[Jod Na Nawood|Silvo]]" and his [[Silvo's pirates|pirates]] were able to find [[At Attin]] when he came across a [[Skeleton Crew|group]] of children at Port Borgo.<ref name="Past the Barrier">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}}</ref> Silvo was able to use the [[Onyx Cinder]] to land on At Attin<ref name="We're Gonna Be In So Much Trouble">{{SkeletonCrew|We're Gonna Be In So Much Trouble}}</ref> and force Under Secretary [[Fara]] to allow his [[Silvo's pirate frigate|frigate]] through the barrier. However, [[SM-33]] and [[KB]] were able to contact [[Kh'ymm]] and she was able to send Commander [[Kent]] and his Squadron of [[New Republic]] X-wings. Silvo was left behind and watched as the New Republic destroyed his frigate.<ref name="Real Good Guys">{{SkeletonCrew|The Real Good Guys}}</ref>

===Age of Resistance===
[[File:CrimsonCorsairCrewRaid-Ashcan.png|thumb|right|250px|Sidon Ithano's crew raiding a Separatist holdout.]]
Pirates such as [[Sidon Ithano]] searched for treasure.<ref name="Lost Treasure of Count Dooku">{{StoryCite|story=The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku|book=Tales from a Galaxy Far, Far Away: Aliens: Volume I}}</ref> During the [[Cold War]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], First Order officer Commander [[Pyre]] and Major [[Elrik Vonreg]] worked with [[Kragan Gorr]] and his [[Warbird gang]] in raiding and attacking the ''[[Colossus]]''. The First Order hoped that this would force Captain [[Imanuel Doza]] in accepting their "help" in protecting the platform from further attacks.<ref name="Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref> Gorr sent [[Synara San]] to infiltrate the ''Colossus'' and spy on them.<ref name="Signal from Sector Six">{{Resistance|Signal from Sector Six}}</ref>

Gorr and a pair of his pirates were able to kidnap Doza's daughter [[Torra Doza]] and took her to their ship. When the First Order arrived, Gorr and his gang were double-crossed and forced to retreat when the [[Ace Squadron]] arrived to assist.<ref name="Doza Dilemma">{{Resistance|The Doza Dilemma}}</ref> Gorr was able to retrieve San after she escaped from the ''Colossus''.<ref name="First Order Occupation">{{Resistance|The First Order Occupation}}</ref> Gorr and his gang then intercepted a transmission to the Resistance from the spy [[Kazuda Xiono]].<ref name="Descent">{{Resistance|Descent (episode)}}</ref> Gorr and his gang assisted the ''Colossus''{{'s}} escape from a [[Thunderer|First Order Star Destroyer]]. They later boarded the ''Colossus'' as it entered hyperspace towards the [[Resistance base]] on [[D'Qar]].<ref name="No Escape 2">{{Resistance|No Escape: Part 2}}</ref>

